cb8-4022da72fc78" 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417216 1080 "III only" 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417216 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417216 1083 #uuid "99e8273a-2cc4-5606-ade8-2988cc10652d" 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417217 1080 "I and IV only" 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417217 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417217 1083 #uuid "a149c6f5-ef3c-51ad-997e-db08bfab777c" 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417218 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417213 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417218 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417214 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417218 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417215 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417218 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417216 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417218 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417217 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417218 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417218 1077 "selection" 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417218 1078 #edb/ref 17592186417214 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417218 1079 #uuid "7336d919-b96c-5024-ae89-e9caaf4e41d0" 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417219 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417218 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417219 1069 "q-156620" 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417219 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417219 1071 "Let $L$ be the line with equation $4x=2y$ in ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $L$ contains the zero-vector\n- $L$ is closed under vector addition\n- $L$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{2}$" 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417219 1072 #uuid "feee3179-e7d1-55ab-bcac-f334cca10495" 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417219 1074 "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $L$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 2x\\end{aligned}],\\,x\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The coordinates of the zero-vector satisfy the equation $4x=2y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =2y \\\\ 4(0) & =2(0) \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 2a\\end{aligned}]\\in L$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ 2b\\end{aligned}]\\in L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 2a\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ 2b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a+b \\\\ 2a+2b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a+b \\\\ 2(a+b)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $4x=2y.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in L.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 2a\\end{aligned}]\\in L$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 2a\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}ka \\\\ k(2a)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}ka \\\\ 2(ka)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich satisfies the condition $4x=2y.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in L.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since statements II and III are true, $L$ must be a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417220 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417224 13194139534281 17592186045417 true] [17592186417220 1062 #uuid "1436249c-5de8-51a2-9062-17b0c4a22818" 13194139534281 1759218604541